00:22:12.440 --> 00:22:13.560
Now, just have your tea.

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:16.820
Alice, we've got some errands for you to do in the village.

00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:19.330
Yes, I won't have it.

00:22:20.210 --> 00:22:22.270
It's probably got sleeping powders in it like the other did.

00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:24.830
Drink your tea, Marion.

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:27.380
Who'd she say you were?

00:22:27.480 --> 00:22:29.120
Well, some woman from some agency.

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:31.700
Last week she said I was the queen.

00:22:32.380 --> 00:22:34.040
Coming down in the world, aren't you?

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:35.800
It's a fair caution.

00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:38.810
If you didn't know she was, well, like she is,

00:22:39.010 --> 00:22:40.590
you'd swear she was telling the truth.

00:22:40.770 --> 00:22:42.970
It's a heavy burden on Mr. Roush and his mother.

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:44.670
They've spent a fortune on doctors.

00:22:44.940 --> 00:22:46.240
Will she always be barmy?

00:22:46.590 --> 00:22:48.450
We just say she's ill.

00:22:49.900 --> 00:22:53.000
And when you go into the village, I don't want you gossiping about the family.

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:56.200
Oh, no, Mrs. Sparks. I'm a close-mouth. I am.

00:22:56.680 --> 00:22:58.080
Of course we don't want to appear.

00:22:58.400 --> 00:22:59.960
Stand off-ish, so you can...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:03.620
answer any questions. Oh, I won't breathe a word about her being balmy.

00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:33.300
Who's there?

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:05.850
Don't come near me! Don't come near me!

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:14.370
Marion, what is it?

00:24:14.990 --> 00:24:15.730
What happened to that?

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:19.080
I threw something at him.

00:24:19.700 --> 00:24:20.220
At whom, dear?

00:24:20.990 --> 00:24:21.710
I thought it was you.

00:24:21.930 --> 00:24:24.050
Darling, I've been asleep. You've had another nightmare.

00:24:24.920 --> 00:24:27.400
But he was real. I saw his eyes right there, glaring at me.

00:24:28.080 --> 00:24:29.260
That's what you saw.

00:24:30.990 --> 00:24:33.380
Why, of course. It was the cat.

00:24:33.800 --> 00:24:36.420
You saw his eyes in the mirror and thought it was someone.

00:24:37.200 --> 00:24:39.360
I saw a man's hand right here on the bed.

00:24:39.970 --> 00:24:41.530
No one could have got into the room.

00:24:41.910 --> 00:24:46.880
I locked the door, in case you walked in your sleep and hurt yourself.

00:24:47.390 --> 00:24:49.190
Then the man must still be in here somewhere.

00:24:49.960 --> 00:24:50.860
Well, you better have a look.

00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:56.280
If no one could get into the room, where did the cat come from?

00:24:57.300 --> 00:24:57.860
Up the window.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.500
and a cat could climb those walls.

00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:11.900
But, see, there's no one here.

00:25:12.330 --> 00:25:13.290
You'd better take the cat away.

00:25:13.570 --> 00:25:14.610
Clear out that glass in the morning.

00:25:14.650 --> 00:25:15.210
Yes, ma'am.

00:25:16.240 --> 00:25:17.160
If you're nervous, Marion,

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:19.820
would you like me to stay the rest of the night with you?

00:25:23.260 --> 00:25:24.580
Why did you bring me here?

00:25:25.630 --> 00:25:27.150
What are you planning to do with me?

00:25:28.380 --> 00:25:29.980
Are you trying to drive me crazy as...

00:25:30.480 --> 00:25:33.560
Tell me what you're planning to do with me.

00:25:34.720 --> 00:25:35.660
Nothing, Marion.

00:25:36.140 --> 00:25:38.860
Nothing but try to make you well, dear. That's all.

00:25:39.610 --> 00:25:41.590
Why don't you leave the light on if you're frightened?

00:25:44.950 --> 00:25:45.330
Good night.

00:25:59.680 --> 00:25:59.980
Oh, uh...

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:01.700
Uh, Mrs. Mackey, anything for me?

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:02.440
Nothing for you.

00:26:02.970 --> 00:26:03.450
Are you sure?

00:26:04.560 --> 00:26:06.300
She ain't had time to write a letter yet.

00:26:06.610 --> 00:26:07.210
It's only mandate.

00:26:07.650 --> 00:26:09.410
You're gonna make yourself late at the office for nothing.

00:26:09.890 --> 00:26:11.910
The legal profession doesn't keep me that busy, Mrs. Mackey.

00:26:12.780 --> 00:26:13.820
She's had three days to explain.

00:26:14.110 --> 00:26:16.850
Oh, women never explain, especially if they're wrong.

00:26:17.030 --> 00:26:19.190
It'll probably come in the afternoon post, uh, here.

00:26:20.060 --> 00:26:20.300
Oh.

00:26:20.440 --> 00:26:22.500
If it does come, this afternoon or any time,

00:26:22.730 --> 00:26:24.030
call me at the office, you know the number,

00:26:24.130 --> 00:26:25.190
and I'll give you another five shillings.

00:26:25.410 --> 00:26:26.350
Oh, thank you.

00:26:27.420 --> 00:26:28.900
Thank you very much, Mr. Bruce.

00:26:30.250 --> 00:26:30.470
You

00:27:02.490 --> 00:27:03.950
Can I take the breakfast tray, Mrs. Hughes?

00:27:05.140 --> 00:27:06.480
Oh, Alice, I didn't hear you.

00:27:07.040 --> 00:27:08.360
Were you looking for something, Mum?

00:27:08.890 --> 00:27:10.410
Is there another entrance to this room?

00:27:10.840 --> 00:27:11.700
Another entrance?

00:27:12.880 --> 00:27:14.680
They'd keep my door locked, but...

00:27:14.680 --> 00:27:17.020
That's to protect you, Mum. Against yourself.

00:27:17.440 --> 00:27:18.720
But someone gets in here.

00:27:19.740 --> 00:27:22.140
Oh, if they want to kill me, why haven't they already done it?

00:27:22.740 --> 00:27:23.360
Headache, Mum?

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:24.780
And why not?

00:27:25.160 --> 00:27:28.180
Sleeping pills to keep me down and prowlers to keep me awake.

00:27:29.460 --> 00:27:29.840
Alice.

00:27:30.350 --> 00:27:32.460
Will you help me? Will you do something for me?

00:27:32.660 --> 00:27:33.660
Of course, Mum.

00:27:34.160 --> 00:27:36.180
If you'd go to the police for me on your day off,

00:27:36.360 --> 00:27:38.060
I'd promise to send your money back from London.

00:27:38.490 --> 00:27:40.050
You're making yourself ill, Mum.

00:27:40.230 --> 00:27:42.430
It's not right, begging your pardon, Mum.

00:27:42.860 --> 00:27:46.280
You have a beautiful home, nice relations, pretty clothes,

00:27:46.740 --> 00:27:48.180
everything a woman would want.

00:27:48.610 --> 00:27:49.390
Oh, nonsense.

00:27:49.630 --> 00:27:50.710
Of course you have, Mum.

00:27:50.990 --> 00:27:53.070
You're letting yourself be took up by illusions,

00:27:53.630 --> 00:27:56.230
letting it gnaw at you and gnaw at you.

00:27:56.570 --> 00:27:57.570
It's all in the mind.

00:27:57.950 --> 00:27:59.630
People can think themselves into anything.

00:28:00.890 --> 00:28:02.670
Why don't you think you're getting well, Mum?

00:28:03.210 --> 00:28:04.450
I tell you, I'm not ill.

00:28:05.400 --> 00:28:07.590
Alice, if you do as I ask...

00:28:07.680 --> 00:28:08.440
You may go, Alice.

00:28:08.640 --> 00:28:08.980
Yes.

00:28:09.670 --> 00:28:11.940
Well, Marion, up and about.

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:14.620
I'll go crazy if you don't let me out of this room.

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:17.100
Forced to drink that tea, my arm all bruised.

00:28:17.500 --> 00:28:17.900
Bruised?

00:28:18.800 --> 00:28:20.080
I'm going to dress and go downstairs.

00:28:20.380 --> 00:28:22.500
Well, of course, dear. No one will stop you.

00:28:22.980 --> 00:28:24.300
The change might do you good.

00:28:26.740 --> 00:28:27.540
My size.

00:28:27.960 --> 00:28:29.920
Naturally. It was made for you.

00:28:30.640 --> 00:28:32.660
You needn't call me Marion when we're alone.

00:28:32.780 --> 00:28:34.820
I know perfectly well you only do it to impress Alice.

00:28:35.720 --> 00:28:38.480
And if there was a Marion Hughes, where is she?

00:28:41.040 --> 00:28:43.400
Do hurry in and come downstairs, dear.

00:29:15.450 --> 00:29:19.180
You must try to be more cautious and not let your temper sway you.

00:29:20.100 --> 00:29:20.980
All right, Mother.

00:29:21.690 --> 00:29:24.070
It's lucky I saw those bruises before someone else did.

00:29:24.580 --> 00:29:26.400
I had to force her to drink the tea, didn't I?

00:29:26.690 --> 00:29:28.270
You don't have to leave evidence.

00:29:31.790 --> 00:29:33.310
Stop it stop it

00:30:05.430 --> 00:30:29.760
Be careful.

00:31:03.930 --> 00:31:09.580
Good morning. I'm Mrs. Hughes. I'm going for a walk. Please open the gate.

00:31:09.980 --> 00:31:11.860
I'm sorry, ma'am, but I got my orders.

00:31:13.510 --> 00:31:16.420
Listen, it's all wrong what they've told you about me.

00:31:17.080 --> 00:31:20.530
I'm not crazy. I don't look crazy, do I?

00:31:20.790 --> 00:31:22.530
Well, nobody ever said that, Mrs. Hughes.

00:31:22.990 --> 00:31:27.140
It's just that you, well, need a bit of looking after, like.

00:31:27.830 --> 00:31:29.050
I'll go and find the house, ma'am.

00:31:29.530 --> 00:31:29.970
They'll be fresh.

00:31:30.060 --> 00:31:31.720
Oh, please don't do that!

00:32:26.940 --> 00:32:27.940
What are you doing away out here?

00:32:28.700 --> 00:32:29.770
I... nothing.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:31.240
I wanted to go for a walk.

00:32:31.400 --> 00:32:33.060
I was just calling the aspers to use.

00:32:33.240 --> 00:32:34.700
Thank you. It's all right now.

00:32:36.090 --> 00:32:37.250
I'd enjoy your walk, too, dear.

00:32:38.200 --> 00:32:39.180
Let's have a look at the grounds.

00:32:44.840 --> 00:32:45.380
Thank you, Evans.

00:32:54.810 --> 00:32:55.050
Yes?

00:32:56.110 --> 00:32:58.750
I've been wondering if maybe you and your mother aren't right about me.

00:33:00.190 --> 00:33:02.710
I've been thinking maybe I really have been ill.

00:33:03.140 --> 00:33:03.820
Have you married?

00:33:04.220 --> 00:33:04.620
Yes.

00:33:05.700 --> 00:33:07.660
So I've been trying to look back and remember things.

00:33:08.040 --> 00:33:10.350
What was my name before we were married?

00:33:11.080 --> 00:33:11.480
Campbell.

00:33:12.510 --> 00:33:13.310
Marion Campbell.

00:33:14.170 --> 00:33:15.090
And what about my family?

00:33:15.170 --> 00:33:15.530
Where are they?

00:33:15.940 --> 00:33:17.220
Your parents are dead, Marion.

00:33:18.600 --> 00:33:19.860
Haven't I any family at all?

00:33:20.540 --> 00:33:21.440
No one to visit me?

00:33:21.480 --> 00:33:21.760
No.

00:33:22.260 --> 00:33:22.920
Or to write?

00:33:26.700 --> 00:33:27.580
Beautiful, isn't it?

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:31.900
Would you like to listen to the sea and hear what it says?

00:33:34.160 --> 00:33:35.480
It doesn't say anything, does it?

00:33:36.280 --> 00:33:37.560
That's what I like about the sea.

00:33:38.920 --> 00:33:40.080
It never tells its secrets.

00:33:41.320 --> 00:33:44.740
And it has many, very many secrets.

00:33:46.920 --> 00:33:47.980
I'd like to go to a doctor.

00:33:48.870 --> 00:33:50.210
Alice says there's a good one in the village.

00:33:50.450 --> 00:33:51.530
I'm sure he could help me.

00:33:51.550 --> 00:33:53.050
You've been to the best specialist in London.

00:33:53.310 --> 00:33:58.810
You know, I'm a very lucky man to find such an attractive wife.

00:33:59.470 --> 00:33:59.970
Where did you find her?

00:34:00.160 --> 00:34:01.300
I can't remember.

00:34:01.480 --> 00:34:01.920
Switzerland?

00:34:02.680 --> 00:34:03.560
What were we doing there?

00:34:03.890 --> 00:34:05.190
I was visiting some people.

00:34:05.250 --> 00:34:05.810
You were in school.

00:34:06.170 --> 00:34:06.570
What school?

00:34:07.580 --> 00:34:10.810
Why not try to remember more pleasant things, like our honeymoon?

00:35:11.870 --> 00:35:16.230
Yes. Someone from the village to see us.

00:35:16.970 --> 00:35:17.910
Tell him not to let them in.

00:35:18.220 --> 00:35:19.880
No, no. Better look out.

00:35:21.620 --> 00:35:23.790
Let them through, Evans. Yes.

00:35:27.570 --> 00:35:29.210
Better keep Marion in a room while they're here.

00:36:17.440 --> 00:36:18.180
I'm glad you got my note.

00:36:24.140 --> 00:36:25.060
You're not a policeman.

00:36:26.040 --> 00:36:27.500
No, I'm afraid not.

00:36:30.890 --> 00:36:33.580
Marion, dear, please. Oh, how do you do?

00:36:33.800 --> 00:36:36.200
I'm Mrs. Hughes. This is my daughter-in-law.

00:36:36.540 --> 00:36:37.780
I'm the vicar, Jonathan Lewis.

00:36:38.080 --> 00:36:40.840
This is my sister, Mrs. Robinson, and her husband.

00:36:41.000 --> 00:36:41.480
How do you do?

00:36:41.720 --> 00:36:43.420
Perhaps we've come calling at a bad time.

00:36:43.540 --> 00:36:45.640
But we did want you to feel that the village welcomes you,

00:36:45.860 --> 00:36:46.820
that you have friendly neighbors.

00:36:47.060 --> 00:36:48.240
Oh, won't you come in?

00:36:48.420 --> 00:36:48.920
Thank you.

00:36:50.800 --> 00:36:53.250
This is my son, Ralph. This is our vicar.

00:36:53.330 --> 00:36:53.870
How do you do?

00:36:54.130 --> 00:36:54.970
Mrs. Robinson.

00:36:55.110 --> 00:36:55.490
How do you do?

00:36:55.590 --> 00:36:55.950
How do you do?

00:36:55.990 --> 00:36:56.710
Mr. Robinson.

00:36:57.390 --> 00:36:57.930
How do you do, sir?

00:36:58.120 --> 00:36:58.640
How do you do?

00:36:59.540 --> 00:36:59.860
Please.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:05.200
listen to me. They're holding me here by force. I don't know why, but you must call the police.

00:37:05.760 --> 00:37:11.040
I'm terribly sorry, but my daughter-in-law is upset today. Ralph, it's so nice of you, Vicar,

00:37:11.040 --> 00:37:15.240
to come and call so promptly. And Mr. and Mrs. Robinson, too. Indeed, the whole village is so

00:37:15.240 --> 00:37:20.820
friendly and charming. We're quite in love with it. No, it's not true. Why doesn't somebody

00:37:20.820 --> 00:37:25.580
listen to me for once instead of believing her all the time? I'm so sorry. I missed going into

00:37:25.580 --> 00:37:29.970
church yesterday. Both my son and I wanted to go, but poor Marion was quite exult.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:34.840
with the journey and we couldn't leave the poor dear alone won't you come and sit down uh mrs

00:37:34.840 --> 00:37:43.640
robertson sit here won't you vicar thank you yes they've already heard about me in the village

00:37:43.640 --> 00:37:49.240
haven't they i suppose so gossip travels very quickly there isn't much they don't know about

00:37:49.240 --> 00:37:53.360
my little wife but there's one thing you don't know the police will be here today and you'd

00:37:53.360 --> 00:37:59.870
better see to it that i'm all right when they come you mean because of this note the one the gate

00:38:00.450 --> 00:38:14.180
Isn't that an awful exhibition? But how did a poor Mrs. Hughes in the face?

00:38:14.420 --> 00:38:17.370
Poor Mr. Hughes, I was thinking. I'll crawl in back.

00:38:17.550 --> 00:38:18.800
There's plenty of room up here, dear.

00:38:20.200 --> 00:38:24.340
The young husband doesn't say much, but you can see he feels it deeply.

00:38:24.640 --> 00:38:27.640
He talks about her in such a gentle way. So touchy.

00:38:49.390 --> 00:38:51.990
Perhaps a rest in a quiet place like this will do her good.

00:38:52.170 --> 00:38:55.030
They made Alice told our cook the poor girl is steadily getting worse,

00:38:55.190 --> 00:38:56.850
though the family refused to admit it.

00:38:57.030 --> 00:38:58.530
Susan, you shouldn't listen to gossip.

00:38:59.030 --> 00:38:59.870
But how did it happen?

00:39:00.380 --> 00:39:05.490
down about a year ago. They've been to every doctor in the country. Jonathan, do be careful

00:39:05.490 --> 00:39:29.970
with those girls. Oh, I forgot to ask Mrs. Hughes something. It won't take a minute.

00:39:35.570 --> 00:39:53.580
I beg your pardon, sir. Have you seen my wife?

00:39:55.130 --> 00:39:57.570
Yes, she's here. You'll find her in the back seat of the car.

00:40:02.240 --> 00:40:05.480
She couldn't have made a better impression for us if we'd planned it ourselves.

00:40:05.920 --> 00:40:08.800
Now, everyone knows she's not responsible for anything she may do.

00:40:09.020 --> 00:40:11.020
Then why don't we get it all over with right now?

00:40:11.100 --> 00:40:14.920
Because there's still one last step, the most important.

00:40:15.560 --> 00:40:16.240
What's that, Mother?

00:40:16.580 --> 00:40:17.780
Our best alibi.

00:40:24.660 --> 00:40:24.840
What?

00:40:29.140 --> 00:40:29.960
That's not a very fact.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.460
a friendly way for a wife to greet her husband.

00:40:32.150 --> 00:40:32.470
Wife?

00:40:33.700 --> 00:40:34.780
Please don't be afraid of me.

00:40:35.900 --> 00:40:37.660
For a while today, I thought we were going to be friends,

00:40:37.920 --> 00:40:38.680
the way we used to be.

00:40:39.840 --> 00:40:41.620
Why don't you stop this farce?

00:40:41.880 --> 00:40:43.760
It's not a farce. I've always loved you, Marion.

00:40:44.650 --> 00:40:46.450
Would it make any difference if I called you Julia?

00:40:47.120 --> 00:40:50.040
Get out of here. Stop!

00:41:06.380 --> 00:41:10.990
Mary, how could you do such it? Mrs. Hughes tried to throw us out of the window.

00:41:11.290 --> 00:41:12.070
Get my mother. Hurry.

00:41:12.740 --> 00:41:13.260
Yes, sir.

00:41:13.910 --> 00:41:16.150
And then get someone from the village to come up here and put some bars on these windows.

00:41:16.800 --> 00:41:18.920
It isn't safe to leave my wife alone any longer. Quick!

00:41:35.310 --> 00:41:37.160
Good morning, Mum. Good morning.

00:41:40.270 --> 00:41:43.010
Goodness, Mum. Didn't you go to bed at all last night?

00:41:43.230 --> 00:41:44.370
No, and why should I?

00:41:45.090 --> 00:41:46.870
I can't sleep and I can't eat either.

00:41:48.350 --> 00:41:50.090
Take that away. Take it away.

00:41:51.710 --> 00:41:52.710
Probably poisoned.

00:41:53.020 --> 00:41:56.020
Oh, no, Mum. You mustn't excite yourself like this.

00:41:56.500 --> 00:41:59.380
Why not? Locked up like an animal with someone trying to kill me.

00:41:59.640 --> 00:41:59.940
Don't.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:06.960
say that, Mum? You're like all the rest of them. What's going on here? She's all upset, Mum. And who

00:42:06.960 --> 00:42:12.470
wouldn't be? How would you like to be in my place? Never allowed out of here for a moment. They're

00:42:12.470 --> 00:42:16.860
afraid to let me out. They're afraid of what I'll tell about them. They don't even dare let me take

00:42:16.860 --> 00:42:20.560
a drive through the village for fear that people will find out how they treat me. They'd love to take

00:42:20.560 --> 00:42:27.390
you out for a drive, Mum, if that's all you want. It's a do her good. Of that, I'm sure. Why, of course.

00:42:27.730 --> 00:42:29.350
I think it's a wonderful idea.

00:42:30.090 --> 00:42:32.570
You can drive along the coast road, up to Observation Point.

00:42:32.830 --> 00:42:34.110
I want Alice to go along, too.

00:42:34.850 --> 00:42:36.430
I have a good deal of work to do, Mum.

00:42:36.780 --> 00:42:37.420
Please, Alice.

00:42:37.560 --> 00:42:39.120
Run along, Alice. Your work can wait.

00:42:39.480 --> 00:42:41.440
Go down and tell Sparks to bring the car round.

00:42:41.890 --> 00:42:44.340
Yes, Mum. I'll be ready in a moment.

00:42:44.480 --> 00:42:45.580
Well, there's no great rush, dear.

00:42:46.040 --> 00:42:47.760
You must give Ralph time to have his breakfast.

00:42:48.080 --> 00:42:52.960
I think it's another scheme to get away.

00:42:53.920 --> 00:42:54.640
Sure it is.

00:43:32.750 --> 00:43:35.210
Now you can let her post it, and no harm done.

00:43:35.830 --> 00:43:37.270
But why let her think she succeeded?

00:43:37.410 --> 00:43:37.830
Why not?

00:43:38.410 --> 00:43:40.190
It's what the villagers think that counts now.

00:43:40.630 --> 00:43:42.730
I want them to see how kind you are to her,

00:43:43.410 --> 00:43:44.450
especially after yesterday.

00:44:31.360 --> 00:44:36.520
You should sit closer so that people can see what a handsome couple we are.

00:44:37.300 --> 00:44:42.600
Shouldn't she, Alice? Riding to someone?

00:44:43.290 --> 00:44:44.510
Yes, a friend in London.

00:44:45.320 --> 00:44:46.120
You haven't sealed it.

00:44:47.220 --> 00:44:50.040
What difference does it make? I know you won't let me send it.

00:44:53.230 --> 00:44:56.630
What an imagination. Why should I stop you?

00:44:57.500 --> 00:44:59.620
As soon as we get to the village, you can post it.

00:45:33.800 --> 00:45:34.640
Good morning, Mr. Hughes.

00:45:34.860 --> 00:45:35.100
Good morning.

00:45:35.320 --> 00:45:36.120
And Mrs. Hughes.

00:45:36.560 --> 00:45:37.640
Nice to see you out.

00:45:38.460 --> 00:45:39.780
And are you feeling a little better today?

00:45:40.120 --> 00:45:41.300
I've never been ill, thank you.

00:45:41.660 --> 00:45:42.900
Uh, give me your letter, dear.

00:45:43.280 --> 00:45:44.140
I'll mail it for you.

00:45:44.360 --> 00:45:45.380
I'd rather mail it myself.

00:45:46.060 --> 00:45:46.880
Good day, Mrs. Robinson.

00:45:47.120 --> 00:45:47.520
Good day?

00:45:50.800 --> 00:45:51.380
Just a moment.

00:45:56.660 --> 00:45:57.880
Wave to Mr. Robinson, dear.

00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:07.060
When will this letter get to London?

00:46:07.670 --> 00:46:08.030
Tomorrow.

00:46:09.070 --> 00:46:10.470
That's fine. Thank you.

00:46:10.750 --> 00:46:11.770
It was a pleasure, my dear.

00:47:31.020 --> 00:47:31.280
Thank you.

00:48:07.770 --> 00:48:09.070
How much longer is it going to be?

00:48:09.830 --> 00:48:11.390
The whole plan had to be convincing.

00:48:12.140 --> 00:48:13.760
Now we can make it look like suicide.

00:48:14.100 --> 00:48:14.500
But when?

00:48:15.390 --> 00:48:15.730
Tonight.

00:48:16.520 --> 00:48:18.580
If by chance that Dennis Bruce should come,

00:48:19.140 --> 00:48:20.380
I don't want us still here.

00:48:20.820 --> 00:48:22.100
How will he find his way here?

00:48:22.500 --> 00:48:23.680
The postmark, of course.

00:48:24.350 --> 00:48:25.250
Postmark on the letter?

00:48:26.470 --> 00:48:27.310
I never thought of that.

00:48:29.060 --> 00:48:29.920
Why did you take the chance?

00:48:30.990 --> 00:48:34.990
It wasn't much of a chance. Nobody in Beveton ever heard of Julia Ross.

00:48:35.650 --> 00:48:41.620
That's true. Nobody but Sparks and Peters. I'd like to throw them in the sea, too.

00:48:42.860 --> 00:48:46.190
Oh, they're all right. We know too much about them.

00:48:47.100 --> 00:48:50.400
It's all Marion's fault. She shouldn't have cried.

00:48:51.300 --> 00:48:55.970
Ralph, you never told me. Was it an accident?

00:48:56.860 --> 00:48:59.970
Or did you intend to kill her after she'd made her way?

00:49:01.340 --> 00:49:03.860
I didn't plan it. I liked her well enough.

00:49:04.910 --> 00:49:07.070
But when she found out I'd been lying about my income,

00:49:07.290 --> 00:49:09.170
she accused me of marrying her for her money.

00:49:10.080 --> 00:49:11.600
I said, of course, that's what I married her for.

00:49:12.620 --> 00:49:15.330
Then she cried. She was always crying.

00:49:16.780 --> 00:49:17.680
Then she slapped me.

00:49:19.000 --> 00:49:21.900
I had my knife in my hand and I...

00:49:25.600 --> 00:49:27.000
Stop it! Stop it!

00:49:27.220 --> 00:49:28.000
Don't do that!

00:49:33.000 --> 00:49:51.840
Put that away, Ralphie. I'm trying to help you.

00:49:52.710 --> 00:49:57.520
I still say we should have called the police and told them a prowler broke in and killed her.

00:49:57.960 --> 00:49:59.680
With the marks of your fingers on her?

00:50:00.830 --> 00:50:02.490
The scratches on your face.

00:50:04.090 --> 00:50:06.680
No, we couldn't let anybody see her.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:33.780
Run downstairs. Tell Sparks to bring egg white, milk, mustard, anything she can think of.

00:51:33.820 --> 00:51:33.960
Yes!

00:51:36.330 --> 00:51:39.150
Why try to save her? Let her die. It's what we want.

00:51:39.270 --> 00:51:40.170
Don't be so stupid, Ralph.

00:51:40.910 --> 00:51:43.650
If she's taking poison, we must act as though we cared.

00:51:44.110 --> 00:51:45.130
If she's taking poison?

00:51:45.730 --> 00:51:47.310
Maybe just a trick to get a doctor here.

00:51:47.700 --> 00:51:48.580
Can't let her see a doctor?

00:51:49.320 --> 00:51:53.550
No. It's easy enough to fool stupid villagers into thinking she's crazy,

00:51:53.570 --> 00:51:55.490
but a doctor would know better.

00:51:56.290 --> 00:51:56.830
What'll we do?

00:51:57.580 --> 00:51:59.980
If she's really taking something, she may...

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:05.900
She may die quickly. If she hasn't, I'll call her a doctor.

00:52:15.520 --> 00:52:18.610
Marion, dear, here's the doctor. He's come to help you.

00:52:21.100 --> 00:52:22.760
I want to speak to the doctor alone. Go away.

00:52:23.900 --> 00:52:24.340
Yes, dear.

00:52:30.990 --> 00:52:34.640
Listen, I haven't taken poison, and I'm not Marion Hughes.

00:52:35.130 --> 00:52:36.750
I'm Julia Ross, and I can prove it.

00:52:37.270 --> 00:52:41.670
If you'd only believe me for just a second and call Dennis Bruce in London, he'll tell you all about me.

00:52:42.380 --> 00:52:43.920
Then you really didn't take anything.

00:52:44.920 --> 00:52:46.220
I just said that to get you here.

00:52:47.530 --> 00:52:48.570
You've got to get me away.

00:52:49.080 --> 00:52:52.980
To a hospital if you think I'm crazy, or anywhere, just to get me away from here.

00:52:55.000 --> 00:52:58.600
I know I sound crazy, but that's what they want everyone to think.

00:52:59.210 --> 00:52:59.970
Because he killed...

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:04.360
his wife and she's lying out there at the bottom of the sea and now they have to have someone to

00:53:04.360 --> 00:53:12.590
bury in her name. What makes you believe all this? You're going to get me away from here for a few

00:53:12.590 --> 00:53:17.830
hours. That's all I ask. Till tomorrow morning. Then Dennis will be here and your responsibility

00:53:17.830 --> 00:53:24.000
will be over. My dear, this is all very puzzling. How do I know that this friend of yours will ever

00:53:24.000 --> 00:53:29.220
get here? A letter off to him. They thought it was just a blank sheet of paper.

00:53:30.220 --> 00:53:33.340
I had a second letter, I thought. I really sent that.

00:53:34.060 --> 00:53:35.020
When did you post it?

00:53:35.500 --> 00:53:37.340
Yesterday. It ought to be there today.

00:53:38.150 --> 00:53:38.970
Enough of that, Peters.

00:53:43.000 --> 00:53:48.140
Yes, then you're not really a duck.

00:53:50.110 --> 00:53:51.270
I told you not to let her post it.

00:53:51.490 --> 00:53:52.450
May not have reached him yet.

00:53:52.710 --> 00:53:55.970
Peters, you must hurry up to London and get that letter before it's delivered.

00:53:56.400 --> 00:53:57.920
Take the car and drive as fast as you can.

00:54:00.090 --> 00:54:00.870
I don't know where he lives.

00:54:00.990 --> 00:54:03.570
Dennis Bruce, 51 Carrington Street, in Romansbury.

00:54:03.630 --> 00:54:04.910
Dennis Bruce, 51 Carrington Street.

00:54:09.730 --> 00:54:11.000
Don't tell her, Mrs. Hughes.

00:54:17.420 --> 00:54:18.300
We're not too late.

00:54:18.500 --> 00:54:18.920
No.

00:54:19.400 --> 00:54:20.680
Did you find out what she took?

00:54:20.860 --> 00:54:23.060
Oh, she didn't really take anything, doctor.

00:54:23.360 --> 00:54:25.780
She admitted that she just meant to frighten us.

00:54:26.360 --> 00:54:28.740
I'm sorry you've had this wild goose chase.

00:54:29.390 --> 00:54:29.830
But...

00:54:31.030 --> 00:54:32.970
Perhaps you'd be good enough to take a look at her.

00:54:33.270 --> 00:54:34.890
You might give her something to calm her.

00:54:35.070 --> 00:54:35.430
Certainly.

00:54:37.730 --> 00:54:39.640
Marion, open the door.

00:54:40.230 --> 00:54:41.470
Go away. I don't want to see anyone.

00:54:42.280 --> 00:54:45.020
But Marion, dear, please, don't be afraid.

00:54:45.380 --> 00:54:46.860
The doctor won't hurt you.

00:54:47.750 --> 00:54:49.290
No, he won't hurt me. He'll just kill me.

00:54:49.670 --> 00:54:51.370
That's what you want him to do. You all want me dead.

00:54:52.120 --> 00:54:54.900
It's hopeless. Hopeless. She'll never recover.

00:54:55.480 --> 00:54:57.240
Oh, doctor, what are we to do?

00:54:57.560 --> 00:54:59.400
She thinks we're on her enemies.

00:54:59.640 --> 00:54:59.980
Try it.

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:05.320
to kill herself she did there's no use trying to see her now she's too upset i suggest taking her

00:55:05.320 --> 00:55:12.340
to the hospital and keeping her under observation for a while oh but uh uh my son refuses to have

00:55:12.340 --> 00:55:18.560
her taken away yes but for her own protection i must try to persuade my son he he's so devoted

00:55:18.560 --> 00:55:23.240
to marion but if if we say it's just for observation then i'll make all the arrangements

00:55:23.360 --> 00:55:29.520
possibly i could come for tonight oh i i think it'd be better if you wait till the morning oh very well

00:55:30.700 --> 00:55:31.900
I hope we can help her.

00:55:32.100 --> 00:55:33.300
I hope so, too, Doctor.

00:55:33.880 --> 00:55:34.200
Goodbye.

00:55:34.680 --> 00:55:35.440
Goodbye, Miss Hughes.

00:55:39.820 --> 00:55:42.910
Ralph, the Doctor will come for her in the morning.

00:55:43.570 --> 00:55:44.170
She'll be ready.

00:56:22.080 --> 00:56:22.540
See you, soldier.

00:56:30.410 --> 00:56:35.670
yes third floor bet 20 shillings a week paid in advance and no cooking I'll take a look at it

00:56:36.240 --> 00:56:39.460
well I'll send the girl up with you because the doctor says I've got to spare myself as much

00:56:39.460 --> 00:56:52.500
as I can you know that girl's never around when she's wanted anyway it's a very tidy room

00:56:52.500 --> 00:56:56.450
and as quiet as a tombstone that's fine I'll take it I don't have to see it the children

00:56:56.450 --> 00:56:59.650
and I will move in tonight yeah what children my two little girls

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:01.420
Oh, you like them. They're full of life.

00:57:01.460 --> 00:57:04.560
Sorry, sorry, but I never take children anyway. The room's taken.

00:57:04.800 --> 00:57:06.980
But I've got to have a room. I've been turned out in my last place.

00:57:07.000 --> 00:57:08.240
Well, you can try and lure down the street.

00:57:08.340 --> 00:57:10.500
Miss Ellingsworth, I think she takes them. It's just around the corner.

00:57:10.660 --> 00:57:12.280
Oh, I'll rush down there at once. Thank you very much.

00:57:14.670 --> 00:57:17.890
Children and dogs. Who ever heard of such a thing?

00:57:19.760 --> 00:57:28.470
Mr. Bloomley, why, that was yet a minute ago.

00:57:30.090 --> 00:57:31.450
Why, there was only him and me.

00:57:32.420 --> 00:57:33.740
Here, wait a minute.

00:58:04.220 --> 00:58:04.360
Thank you.

00:59:33.260 --> 00:59:37.760
Who are you? Are you calling me to him?

00:59:41.770 --> 00:59:42.130
Yes, sir.

01:00:52.200 --> 01:00:53.020
She'd be too excited.

01:01:17.340 --> 01:01:23.740
trouble now this happened and frightened we have nothing to fear we'll be telling

01:01:23.740 --> 01:01:29.260
the truth when we say it's suicide yes who's the weak one now

01:01:31.310 --> 01:01:32.250
Come, let's go down there.

01:01:53.250 --> 01:01:55.580
Mrs. Hughes, I've had an emergency call,

01:01:55.680 --> 01:01:57.440
which will take me away all day tomorrow.

01:01:57.680 --> 01:01:58.700
I'm so glad you're here.

01:01:59.100 --> 01:01:59.980
She must have heard us talk.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:04.100
about taking her away. She's always threatened to kill herself before she'd be locked up.

01:02:04.500 --> 01:02:06.280
She hasn't. Yes, and I blame myself.

01:02:06.850 --> 01:02:08.690
Well, she'll be all standing here talking and doing nothing.

01:02:12.700 --> 01:02:15.800
Nurse, I'll go on down with them. You telephone for an ambulance.

01:02:16.060 --> 01:02:22.690
Yes, doctor. Hurry, down there before the doctor does.

01:02:22.910 --> 01:02:25.610
She'll surely be dead, but just in case she isn't.

01:02:31.310 --> 01:02:32.210
Come along, Mrs. Hughes.

01:02:32.310 --> 01:02:32.690
Yes, thank you.

01:03:23.390 --> 01:03:27.120
see just what you were going to do when you found her there alone. I don't understand.

01:03:31.410 --> 01:03:34.310
No, I only threw my robe over to make you think I jumped.

01:03:34.980 --> 01:03:36.480
Then I got out through the secret door.

01:03:36.840 --> 01:03:38.060
It's luck if you met her on the road.

01:03:41.030 --> 01:03:42.410
I don't know what to say.

01:03:42.830 --> 01:03:44.930
There's nothing for you to say. You're both under arrest.

01:03:45.400 --> 01:03:46.320
We caught Peters in London.

01:03:46.820 --> 01:03:47.220
Peters?

01:03:47.660 --> 01:03:47.980
Yes.

01:03:54.480 --> 01:03:54.680
No!

01:04:28.764 --> 01:04:29.784
Time I apply for a job.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:30.820
I'll ask for the references.

01:04:31.280 --> 01:04:32.430
I know a good job.

01:04:32.740 --> 01:04:33.180
Secretary?

01:04:33.650 --> 01:04:34.290
Oh, a combination.

01:04:34.710 --> 01:04:36.870
Secretary, nurse, companion, housekeeper.

01:04:36.870 --> 01:04:37.490
That sounds like a wife.

01:04:37.830 --> 01:04:39.230
Well, how about it?

01:04:39.840 --> 01:04:41.680
I'll have to have some time to think it over.

01:04:41.900 --> 01:04:42.420
How long?

01:04:42.840 --> 01:04:44.000
Oh, about five seconds.

01:04:44.240 --> 01:04:44.660
One.

01:04:45.060 --> 01:04:46.340
Two, three, four.
